 A multidimensional experience</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>Canada: Ontario University</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yeh</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><source>Loneliness, Alcohol and Marihuana Use among Male College Students</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>University of Conneticut</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>Carver</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Snyder R, Forsyth DR</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Adjustment and coping implications of loneliness</article-title><source>Handbook of social and clinical psychology: The healthy perspective</source><year>1991</year><publisher-name>New York: Pergamon Press</publisher-name><fpage>395</fpage><lpage>415</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deniz</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamarta</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ari</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An investigation of social skills and loneliness levels of university students with respect to their attachment styles in a sample of Turkish students</article-title><source>Social Behaviour and Personality</source><year>2005</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2224/sbp.2005.33.1.19</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ponzetti</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Loneliness among college students</a